            <ArticleTitle>Straddling patent foramen ovale thrombus associated with pulmonary embolism managed with thrombolysis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>365-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A straddling patent foramen ovale thrombus protruding into both atria and ventricles is rare. We hereby describe a case of an acutely ill young male with deep Venous Thrombosis and sub massive pulmonary embolism with a large straddling patent foramen ovale thrombus detected on echocardiography and effectively dissolved with chemical lysis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
